            <ArticleTitle>Effect of mid-dorsal caudate nucleus on conditioning for pain stimulus in rats.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>61-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Male rats were subjected to conditioning, with light source as conditioned stimulus, followed by a noxious stimulus applied to the tail as unconditioned stimulus. There was development of conditioned response after a few days, which was inhibited later on.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
